  font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;font-size:12px;pointer-events:none;
  background:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);color:#f1f5f9;
  box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.18);max-width:260px;z-index:999;
  line-height:1.4;
"></div>
<script>
(function(){
  var tip=document.currentScript.parentElement.querySelector('#ec-tooltip-8');
  var svg=document.currentScript.parentElement.querySelector('svg');
  if(!svg||!tip) return;
  function show(el,ev){
    var raw=el.getAttribute('data-attrs');
    if(!raw) return;
    try{var d=JSON.parse(raw)}catch(e){return}
    var h='';
    for(var k in d){
      var v=d[k];
      if(typeof v==='number'&&!Number.isInteger(v)) v=v.toFixed(4);
      h+='<div><b>'+k+'</b>: '+v+'</div>';
    }
    if(!h) return;
    tip.innerHTML=h;tip.style.display='block';
    var r=svg.getBoundingClientRect();
    tip.style.left=(ev.clientX-r.left+12)+'px';
    tip.style.top=(ev.clientY-r.top-10)+'px';
  }
  svg.addEventListener('mouseover',function(ev){
    var t=ev.target;
    if(t.hasAttribute('data-node')||t.hasAttribute('data-edge')) show(t,ev);
  });
  svg.addEventListener('mousemove',function(ev){
    var r=svg.getBoundingClientRect();
    tip.style.left=(ev.clientX-r.left+12)+'px';
    tip.style.top=(ev.clientY-r.top-10)+'px';
  });
  svg.addEventListener('mouseout',function(ev){
    var t=ev.target;
    if(t.hasAttribute('data-node')||t.hasAttribute('data-edge'))
      tip.style.display='none';
  });
})();
</script>
</div>
```
:::
:::


The women are on the left and the fourteen social events on the right. Without `nodes=`, the
method splits the graph into two sides itself, and raises an error if the graph is not bipartite.

## Circles and shells

[`layout_circular()`](../reference/Graph.layout_circular.qmd) places the nodes evenly around a
circle in the order of their IDs. Since the edges play no part, the picture shows how the order
relates to the structure. In the karate club, whose members are numbered in no meaningful order,
the edges cross the circle in every direction:

::: {#60873f81 .cell execution_count=12}
``` {.python .cell-code}
karate.layout_circular()
karate.plot(layout="pos", color_by="faction", show_labels=False, node_size=8, width=400, height=400)
```

